# Context (reentrant) input — the generated highest default (besluit 6)

A `context` variable of a subscope carries the callee's OWN default, and
the caller MAY override it. Reading B (Catala's C-Def): the caller's value
is the HIGHEST-priority exception — it beats the callee's own computation.
The plugin lowers this to a **generated highest default** above the callee's own
defaults on that target (PHASE5-CATALA decision 6): the default's guard and value
read the caller, navigated over the synthesised back-link (callee → caller),
with no standing machinery — Reading B expressed as default order.

Both polarities ride one program: the caller overrides `drempel` under a
case boolean, so `pas_toe` = true makes the highest default decide (the override
wins) and `pas_toe` = false lets the callee's own base default decide.
Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  context drempel content integer
  output uitkomst content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition drempel equals 10
  definition uitkomst equals grondslag - drempel

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslag content integer
  input eigen_drempel content integer
  input pas_toe content boolean
  kamer scope Kamer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition kamer.grondslag equals grondslag
  definition kamer.drempel under condition pas_toe consequence equals eigen_drempel
  definition heffing equals kamer.uitkomst
```
